  "notes": "Written with {空|あ} (empty) to distinguish from the other あける verbs.\n\nTHREE あける VERBS:\n- {空|あ}ける: to empty, to vacate (this entry)\n- {開|あ}ける: to open (a door, lid, etc.)\n- {明|あ}ける: to dawn, for a period to end\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {空|あ}く (intransitive — to become empty/available)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {席|せき}を{空|あ}ける: to vacate a seat\n- {家|いえ}を{空|あ}ける: to be away from home\n- {時間|じかん}を{空|あ}ける: to make time available\n- {場所|ばしょ}を{空|あ}ける: to clear a space\n- {予定|よてい}を{空|あ}けておく: to keep one's schedule open",
